For Structures/Classes:
=======================
template class A<uint64_t>;

This is how you force a template to be instantiated for a type without allocating object storage for it.
Useful in Libraries.

For Methods:
============
template <class T> int function_name(T a) {}
template int function_name<int>(int);


The key being use template and not template <> when explicitly instantiating a type for the linker to know
